          %title Lipschitz maps
          %h1#lipschitz_maps Lipschitz maps
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definitions"} Definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %li
                %a{:href => "#generalisations"} Generalisations
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_pages"} Related pages
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Lipschitz maps are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            that lie intermediate between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+continuous+maps"} uniformly continuous maps
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+maps"} short maps
          %p
            One can also consider Lipschitz maps between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+spaces"} gauge spaces
            with appropriate gauges, or between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            with appropriate atlases.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            (with the metric denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            for both). Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          #Lipnorm.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong Lipschitz norm
              or
              %strong Lipschitz modulus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi Lip
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f\|_{Lip}}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
              of the absolute
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/difference+quotient"} difference quotient
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{d(f(a), f(b))} {d(a, b)}
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≠
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \neq b
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            In general, this supremum is a
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+real+number"} lower real number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, \infty]
            of nonnegative lower reals, so that the Lipschitz norm is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingleton"} subsingleton
            (so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \neq b
            never occurs).
          #Lipmap.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %strong Lipschitz continuous
              = succeed "," do
                %strong Lipschitz
          %p We can be more specific:
          #specmaps.num_defn
            %h6#definitions_2 Definitions
            %p
              The map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
              is
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+map"} short
              if its Lipschitz norm is at most
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              %strong
                %span.newWikiWord
                  contraction mapping
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/contraction+mapping"} ?
              if its Lipschitz norm is strictly less than
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \in [0, \infty]
            a
            %strong Lipschitz constant
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            if
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi K
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(f(a), f(b)) \leq K d(a, b)
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b\colon X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimum"} minimum
            of the Lipschitz constants (which is always attained, if there is any finite Lipschitz constant at all). In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+real"} upper real
            that is (in general) too large. (For example, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            be the sequence of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+sum"} partial sum
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Specker+sequence"} Specker sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} \subseteq \mathbb{R}
            to
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
          %p
            If you want a definition that is constructively acceptable and yet involves no division, then take the Lipschitz norm of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to be the supremum over those
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi k
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(f(a), f(b)) \gt k d(a, b)
          %p
            for some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b\colon X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0, \infty]
            a priori, and pseudometric spaces, even constructively.) You can even restrict attention to (say)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+number"} rational
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b
            in some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subspace"} dense subspace
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (say if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+space"} separable
          %p
            Every Lipschitz map is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniformly+continuous+map"} uniformly continuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+line"} real line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            to itself is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolutely+continuous+map"} absolutely continuous
          %p
            If a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            between the real line and itself is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+map"} differentiable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum+norm"} supremum norm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f'\|_\infty}
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
            %span.newWikiWord
              Rademacher's theorem
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Rademacher%27s+theorem"} ?
            and its generalisations.)
          %h2#generalisations Generalisations
          %p
            The definitions above generalise immediately to
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasimetric+spaces"} quasimetric spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            is the same as that of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^op\colon X^op \to Y^op
            (although the map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^op
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^op
          %p
            The definitions also generalise to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudometric+spaces"} pseudometric spaces
            if we take the supremum over those
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \neq b
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(a, b) \gt 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(f(a), f(b)) = 0
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(a, b) = 0
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+space"} gauge space
            %em gauge
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "'s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %strong Lipschitz gauge
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is Lipschitz continuous as a map between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with any two of its pseudometrics. Then we may extend
            = succeed "'s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (so equipped) is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Lipschitz gauge space
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with a compatible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
            whose transition maps are all Lipschitz (a
            = succeed ")." do
              %strong Lipschitz atlas
            = succeed "'s" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (so equipped) is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong Lipschitz manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"} paracompact
          %p
            A map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                Lipschitz of order
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                Hölder of order
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi b
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{d(f(a), f(b))} {d(a, b)^\alpha}
          %p
            is finite. Here,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            may be any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive number
            (but is typically taken to be less than
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is simply a Lipschitz map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\alpha
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^\alpha
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with all distances raised to the power of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          %p
            Lipschitz (and Hölder) maps also have non-uniform versions (fix
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood"} neighbourhood
            on which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is Lipschitz). I kind of get lost in all of the possibilities.
